# Romaji sequences for the jprom(kana) NumLock-gated overlay.
# Generated by .config/xkb/gen_kana.py - edit the script, not this file.
# Markers: one hole-free block in this order from U+E001
# (hiragana); the katakana block mirrors it, punctuation follows.
#   a i u e o k s š z ž t d n p h g m j y r w b c č f v -
# The same markers sit on the same czech QWERTZ positions
# on both the US romaji and the czech layout.
# Spelling follows czech pronunciation; the sections are the spec.
# A doubled first letter or the pause key gives っ.
# An apostrophe commits the bare consonant.
# A lone n joins the next kana as ん unless an nV spelling exists.
# Shift on the dash keys smallifies the next spelling.
# The dash key directly after the starter gives っ.
# Foreign sounds extend the same scheme.
# Base vowels never compose: they commit their kana at once.
include "%L"

